import lib/lsp.dl

to get the LSP generic message test interpreter:
    return "python" if the process platform is Windows, else "python3"

set script to "import json,sys\ndef read():\n h={}\n while True:\n  line=sys.stdin.buffer.readline()\n  if line==b'\\r\\n': break\n  n,v=line.decode('ascii').split(':',1);h[n.lower()]=v.strip()\n return json.loads(sys.stdin.buffer.read(int(h['content-length'])))\ndef send(m):\n p=json.dumps(m,separators=(',',':')).encode();sys.stdout.buffer.write(b'Content-Length: '+str(len(p)).encode()+b'\\r\\n\\r\\n'+p);sys.stdout.buffer.flush()\ninit=read();assert init['method']=='initialize';send({'jsonrpc':'2.0','method':'window/logMessage','params':{'type':3,'message':'starting'}});send({'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':init['id'],'result':{'capabilities':{}}});assert read()['method']=='initialized'\nnote=read();assert note['method']=='custom/note' and note['params']=={'value':7}\necho=read();assert echo['method']=='custom/echo' and echo['params']=={'text':'hello'};send({'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':echo['id'],'result':{'text':'hello'}})\ncustom=read();assert custom['method']=='custom/identified' and custom['id']==41 and custom['params']=={'value':41};send({'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':41,'result':{'value':41}})\ncustom=read();assert custom['method']=='custom/string-id' and custom['id']=='chosen' and 'params' not in custom;send({'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':'chosen','result':None})\npending=read();assert pending['method']=='custom/pending' and 'params' not in pending\ncancel=read();assert cancel['method']=='$/cancelRequest' and cancel['params']['id']==pending['id'];send({'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':pending['id'],'error':{'code':-32800,'message':'cancelled'}})\nsend({'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':7,'method':'custom/get','params':{'value':9}});reply=read();assert reply['id']==7 and reply['result']=={'accepted':True}\nsend({'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':'abc','method':'custom/fail','params':{}});reply=read();assert reply['id']=='abc' and reply['error']=={'code':-32602,'message':'bad input','data':{'field':'value'}}\nsend({'jsonrpc':'2.0','method':'custom/event','params':{'ready':True}})\nsend({'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':'unknown','result':None})\nshutdown=read();assert shutdown['method']=='shutdown';send({'jsonrpc':'2.0','id':shutdown['id'],'result':None});assert read()['method']=='exit'"
set command to a process command for the LSP generic message test interpreter
add "-u" as an argument to command
add "-c" as an argument to command
add script as an argument to command

set started to the result of starting an LSP client using command waiting up to 2000 milliseconds
print line started succeeded
set client to started's client

set pumped to the result of pumping one LSP message using client waiting up to 0 milliseconds
print line pumped succeeded
set startup to the next LSP notification from client
print lines (startup succeeded) and (the JSON text named "method" in startup's message = "window/logMessage")
free startup

set opened to the result of opening LSP document "file:///no-sync.dl" written in "dynlex" with "one" as its text using client
print line opened succeeded
set edited to the result of editing LSP document uri "file:///no-sync.dl" from line 0 and character 0 to line 0 and character 3 with text "two" using client
print line edited succeeded
set document to the LSP document with uri "file:///no-sync.dl" in client
print line (document's text = "two")
set closed to the result of closing LSP document uri "file:///no-sync.dl" using client
print line closed succeeded

set note to a new JSON-RPC object
add JSON-RPC member "value" containing a new JSON-RPC integer for 7 to note
set noted to the result of sending an LSP notification "custom/note" with note using client
free note
print line noted succeeded

set parameters to a new JSON-RPC object
add JSON-RPC member "text" containing a new JSON-RPC text for "hello" to parameters
set echoed to the result of sending an LSP request "custom/echo" with parameters using client
free parameters
print line echoed succeeded
set unavailable to the queued LSP response for echoed's request identifier using client
print lines (unavailable failed) and (unavailable's status = the JSON-RPC queue empty status)
free unavailable
set pumped to the result of pumping one LSP message using client waiting up to 2000 milliseconds
print line pumped succeeded
set echo to the queued LSP response for echoed's request identifier using client
print lines (echo succeeded) and (the JSON text named "text" in echo's result = "hello")
free echo

set parameters to a new JSON-RPC object
add JSON-RPC member "value" containing a new JSON-RPC integer for 41 to parameters
set number to a new JSON-RPC integer for 41
set custom to the result of sending an LSP request "custom/identified" with parameters identified by number using client
free parameters
free number
print line custom succeeded
set response to the LSP response for custom's request identifier using client waiting up to 2000 milliseconds
print line response succeeded
set value to the JSON member named "value" in response's result
print line (the number of value = 41.0)
free response

set label to a new JSON-RPC text for "chosen"
set chosen to the result of sending an LSP request "custom/string-id" identified by label using client
free label
print line chosen succeeded
set selection to the LSP response for chosen's request identifier using client waiting up to 2000 milliseconds
print lines (selection succeeded) and (selection's result is JSON null)
free selection

set pending to the result of sending an LSP request "custom/pending" using client
print line pending succeeded
set cancelled to the result of cancelling LSP request pending's request identifier using client
print line cancelled succeeded
set cancellation to the LSP response for pending's request identifier using client waiting up to 2000 milliseconds
print lines (cancellation failed) and (cancellation's status = the JSON-RPC remote error status)
print line (cancellation's remote error code = the LSP request cancelled code)
free cancellation

set pumped to the result of pumping one LSP message using client waiting up to 2000 milliseconds
print line pumped succeeded
set request to the next LSP server request from client
print line request succeeded
set accepted to a new JSON-RPC object
add JSON-RPC member "accepted" containing a new JSON-RPC boolean for true to accepted
set replied to the result of replying to request's message from the LSP server with accepted using client
free accepted
print line replied succeeded
free request

set pumped to the result of pumping one LSP message using client waiting up to 2000 milliseconds
print line pumped succeeded
set failing to the next LSP server request from client
print line failing succeeded
set details to a new JSON-RPC object
add JSON-RPC member "field" containing a new JSON-RPC text for "value" to details
set replied to the result of replying to failing's message from the LSP server with error code the JSON-RPC invalid parameters code message "bad input" and data details using client
free details
print line replied succeeded
free failing

set pumped to the result of pumping one LSP message using client waiting up to 2000 milliseconds
print line pumped succeeded
set event to the next LSP notification from client
print lines (event succeeded) and (the JSON text named "method" in event's message = "custom/event")
free event

set protocol to the result of pumping one LSP message using client waiting up to 2000 milliseconds
print lines (protocol failed) and (protocol's status = the JSON-RPC protocol error status)
set diagnostic to the next LSP protocol diagnostic from client
print lines (diagnostic succeeded) and (diagnostic's error message = "JSON-RPC response has an unknown ID")
print line (the JSON text named "id" in diagnostic's message = "unknown")
free diagnostic

set stopped to the result of shutting down client waiting up to 2000 milliseconds
print line stopped succeeded
free client
